  "TITLE": "Entropy: The Ceiling<br>Every Real Process Hits",
  "LEAD": "The second law of thermodynamics says every real energy conversion generates entropy &mdash; some usable energy is always degraded into a less useful form, so no real heat engine, compressor, or turbine can reach 100% efficiency, or even its own theoretical (Carnot) ceiling. Of the energy that goes in, part becomes useful work, part is lost to avoidable inefficiencies (friction, poor design, fouling), and a third part is lost no matter how well the equipment is built &mdash; that's the entropy tax the second law charges on every real process. Chasing down the avoidable middle slice, not chasing 100%, is the actual efficiency target for real plant equipment.",
